Subject: AI_AB_TEST: every strike list puts a Warrior before its first Settler
 or Worker (Personality)

Economy, for the lead (2026-11-07, why lists run 40-60 turns late):
- Persia 18DA3905: the default list Worker, Settler, Settler, Immortal. Barbarians captured 5 Workers and 3 Settlers
  T12-T87, and Persia had 1 city until T110 while the list rebuilt the same civilians.
- Greece 18BE1E3E: Monument, Settler, Settler, Hoplite. It lost a Worker at T27 and a Settler at T34, and had 1 city
  to about T55.
The ordered list puts a unit that needs a tech (the Hoplite at Bronze Working) after its research item, and the executor
passes over it until then, so the civilians go out alone.
New AddStrikeGuard, the last step of CompleteStrikeLists: unless a combat unit trainable from the start (no prerequisite
tech, not a Scout) is already ahead of the first Settler or Worker, the civ's Warrior goes in just before it (the
Aztecs' Jaguar). Every list, expert and default; a full list drops its last item. Game data only, multiplayer-safe.
Economy's executor backstop (a civilian gives way while barbarians are near and the capital's area has no combat unit)
is separate.

LEAD: every strike list now has a Warrior before its first Settler or Worker (Persia 18DA3905, Greece 18BE1E3E). ai/personality = ai/war 993343d6 + this commit, CI pending; War merges.

